#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133830 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133645 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Line Integral of a Scalar Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8bf6a863-9b9f-5877-84bc-3e11d71261c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6308" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_{C}xy\\,\\textrm{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = 3t\\,\\mathbf{i}+4t\\,\\mathbf{j}\\,$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t) = 3t\\,\\mathbf{i}+4t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ then along the curve we have $x=3t$ and $y=4t.$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y) =xy,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3t\\cdot 4t \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}12{t}^{2}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60{[\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =20{[{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520729 :question-generator/id #uuid "c0ba764f-e619-52a5-9c5c-c72c87ea6af4" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186133830.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Line Integral of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c13ee6c3-92c9-5a3d-b1c3-cc0e6dc9c11d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{96}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131702} {:answer/id #uuid "dd83dc0f-ae75-597e-9bf5-97ca5882c46e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131703} {:answer/id #uuid "23b2b615-b99c-50e0-a324-227c7235fe42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{104}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131704} {:answer/id #uuid "442792c7-4dbd-5bc7-83a1-8c1fbcc8e6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131705} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3b94ad-f1e1-5a06-b9fd-7ea4ca4724ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131706}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ae85dffa-91e2-5047-afe6-7098bbee9ba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131701}] :question/id #uuid "b920de5e-825e-5dcf-9aac-175e4a51e8a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40258" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x, y) = 3x$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t) = ⟨\\frac{4t^{3/2}}{3}, \\frac{t^{2}}{2} - t⟩$ for $t ∈ [0, 1]$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Line Integral of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "867e1617-e